; -*- mode: lisp -*-
; TRIAL 21 of 30 in the tray_pair_both layout sweep: the whole tray
; arrangement yawed -13.4 deg about the goal syringe and shifted by
; (-0.0060, +0.0356) m in the bench plane; the sharps box shifted by
; (-0.0253, +0.0092) m. All drawn from numpy default_rng(seed=0):
; shift uniform(+-0.06) m, yaw uniform(+-25.0) deg, box uniform(+-0.03) m.
; Written by tasks/syringe_packing/tools/make_sweeps.py from tray_pair_both.task; the
; layout is poses/tray_pair_both_t21.json. Everything else is the base document's.
; AUTHORED, over the `syringe` export, as `tray_pair`
; with its goal widened to BOTH syringes (level 1 of the packing work). That
; document's goal is one syringe posted through the sharps box's aperture,
; under the same reproduction binding -- and what this document adds is the
; SCENE: the syringe lies in VAB-industrial's instrument tray beside one
; identical spare, instead of alone on the bare workbench.
;
; WHY A SPARE, AND WHY ONLY ONE. VAB-industrial's own
; `put_ten_syringes_in_the_sharps_box.bddl` racks ten and asks for all ten. Ten
; identical barrels defeated the perception graph -- ten detections are one
; ambiguity per neighbour, and the grasp went to a mid-row neighbour 160 mm
; from the goal -- and looping the routine and the graph over ten would be a
; different task. One spare, 90 mm from the goal along the tray's long axis,
; keeps the packing-work read of the scene without staging that ambiguity:
; an open Panda's fingers sweep +/-37 mm plus a pad, so anything nearer than
; ~58 mm catches a fingertip on the descent, and 90 mm is 66 mm of clear air
; between 23.6 mm barrels. The spare is scenery to the goal: it is declared so
; the scene says what is in it, and no clause reads it.
;
; WHERE THINGS ARE. BDDL has no coordinates. `poses/tray_pair.json` is
; the layout (:start-poses ...) names: the goal syringe at the export's own settled
; pose lifted onto the tray's floor, the spare one spacing along the row, the
; tray yawed a quarter turn from the syringe's heading so its 400 mm axis
; carries the pair, centred on their midpoint. That file was recorded from
; the loader that used to compute all of this at build, and is the layout the
; validated episode ran on (outputs/ten_syringes-rerun-20260909b, reward 1.0).
;
; THE TRAY DOES NOT COLLIDE AS DRAWN. Its MJCF collides as the mesh's convex
; hull, which fills the pan solid; the suite stands an invisible floor slab and
; four walls inside the cavity instead, the way VAB-industrial's own environment
; builds box colliders against the mesh's cavity sites. Until 2026-09-15 the
; slab was the whole of it -- and it sat 6 mm high, level with the rim -- so
; syringes floated over a pan they could also be pushed straight out of. See
; records.py.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(define (problem DISPOSE_BOTH_SYRINGES_FROM_THE_TRAY_T21)
  (:domain robosuite)

  (:language pick up each syringe from the instrument tray, one at a time, and
             drop it through the hole in the top of the yellow sharps disposal
             box, until both are in the box)

  (:staging
    (:profile sharps_vab_industrial@v1)
    ; The same dumped scene `syringe` builds from: bins, bench, sharps box and
    ; the goal syringe's settled pose. The tray and the spare are not in it;
    ; they arrive from the loader at the poses named above.
    ; The export's own free body is dropped: it carries the syringe's authored
    ; box collider, and every syringe here arrives from `records.syringe` --
    ; the same mesh, colliding on its CoACD hulls.
    (:export vab_tool_sort/syringe (:strip-free-bodies true))
    ; Where every free body and the tray stand: recorded, with each
    ; handle's own fields (each syringe's mass and grip, a spare's colour).
    ; What a syringe is *made of* -- the drawn mesh, its map, and the CoACD
    ; hulls it collides on -- is records.py's, stated once.
    (:start-poses poses/tray_pair_both_t21.json)
    ; Two container goals: the single-syringe document's 11400 (2400 for the
    ; goal plus a flat 9000 for a container goal, retried once) for each
    ; syringe. Measured: one posting is 3500-5200 control steps.
    (:max-steps 22800)
    ; A wave builds tray_pair_base's model for this document; the
    ; serial runner ignores this and builds its own, which stays the reference.
    (:fleet-base syringe_packing/tray_pair_base)
  )

  (:fixtures
    bin1 - robosuite_bin
    bin2 - robosuite_bin
    ; Welded into bin2 as geometry rather than a body of its own, so it has a
    ; frame and no handle. The export records the offset.
    syringe_box - sharps_box
  )

  (:objects
    syringe_0 syringe_pack_0 - syringe
  )

  ; Regions are stated in their target's OWN frame, in metres, as
  ; (x0 y0 x1 y1), exactly as `put_the_syringe_in_the_sharps_box` states them.
  (:regions
    (bin1_region
        (:target bin1)
        (:ranges ((-0.18 -0.23 0.18 0.23)))
    )
    (bin2_syringe_region
        (:target bin2)
        (:ranges ((0.0 -0.245 0.195 0.0)))
    )
    (syringe_box_region
        (:target syringe_box)
        (:ranges ((-0.069782 -0.073843 0.019218 0.092157)))
        ; The box this trial moved by (-0.025282, +0.009157) m in bin2; the aperture's
        ; frame is the export's, so the ranges carry the move.
    )
  )

  ; No init constraint: both syringes start in the tray where the layout puts
  ; them, and an init is verified after settling -- stating one the export did
  ; not dump would be stating something unverified.
  (:init)

  ; Both syringes, in any order. Level 1 of the packing work: the spare is
  ; no longer scenery -- the graph loops the same perceive/grasp/carry/post
  ; pipeline over every syringe left in the tray, and this goal is what
  ; scores it. The scene, layout and regions are the single-syringe
  ; document's, so the 30-layout sweep of that document applies here as is.
  (:goal
    (and
      (In syringe_0 syringe_box_region)
      (In syringe_pack_0 syringe_box_region)
    )
  )

  (:artifacts
    (:routine "routine:RoutineSharpsDisposal")
    (:tools   "tools:register_syringe_packing_tools")
    (:graph gt "graphs/gt")
    (:graph gap_perception "graphs/gap_perception")
  )

  (:hosts
    ; The same arena with the Panda cut out of it, hosting a YAM: the export
    ; welds its robot into the room, so a foreign one needs the stripped file.
    (:host (:embodiment yam_i2rt (:work-arm right) (:support-arm left))
           (:static-override workcell scene_norobot_boxm0p0250p009.xml)
           (:notes "compiles; no policy"))
    ; The stripped arena hosting the six-jointed arm, its hand welded on.
    (:host (:embodiment ur5 (:work-arm right))
           (:static-override workcell scene_norobot_boxm0p0250p009.xml)
           (:notes "compiles; no policy"))
    ; The same robot wearing the i2rt gripper -- the fourth axis, taking a value.
    (:host (:embodiment ur5 (:work-arm right)) (:gripper linear_4310_attached)
           (:static-override workcell scene_norobot_boxm0p0250p009.xml)
           (:notes "compiles; no policy"))
    ; The export's own Panda wearing a Robotiq 2F-85: `panda_robotiq`, a
    ; registered embodiment over the hand-free standalone asset.
    (:host (:embodiment panda_robotiq (:work-arm right))
           (:static-override workcell scene_norobot_boxm0p0250p009.xml)
           (:graphs gap_perception)
           (:notes "the reference pairing: gap_perception runs here"))
  )
  (:provenance
    (:tier original)
    (:source "Authored for this corpus over the AUTOLab-GaP-NVIDIA-Collaboration/
              VAB-industrial ToolSortPickPlace `syringe` export (robosuite 1.4.0,
              MuJoCo 3.3.3, seed 0). The goal and regions are
              put_the_syringe_in_the_sharps_box's; the tray and the spare restate
              the scenery of VAB-industrial's put_ten_syringes_in_the_sharps_box
              without its all-ten goal.")
    (:note "Formerly the loader-only variant `ten_syringes`, which aliased the
            single-syringe document and built the tray and the spare in Python.
            The instrument tray mesh is VAB-industrial's own (add-all-syringes-
            sharps-box branch, assets/objects/_utils/make_tray.py), vendored
            under assets/instrument_tray.")
  )
)
